    "title": "NAZA trailer takes to Tel Aviv rooftops for unprecedented view of mass killing - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Matt Schimkowitz ,\n1 days ago After facing life-threatening blowback for their previous film, No Other Land, which saw members of the four-person filmmaking team kidnapped by Israeli soldiers, directors Yuval Abraham and Rachel Szor return home for an unprecedented view of Israel’s Gaza genocide. NAZA, the new film from Abraham and Szor, is a collection of interviews with Israeli whistleblowers from the military and intelligence community. Shot from the rooftops of Tel Aviv in the dead of night, the filmmakers learn about the allotted number of civilian casualties the IDF accepts in its bombardments, a number that seemingly has no limit. The first trailer for NAZA brings viewers to those heights to see the real lows of humanity. Here’s how the directors describe their mission: Read full article",
